// Income `withholding` is the derived withholding (read-only, ADR-0008). **0.12.0 (WH-11, ADR-0008 amendment):** `counterparty_type` is removed; `counterparty_kind`, `operation_kind`, `residential_rent`, `via_platform` and `withholding` are required. Every income written since 0.11.3 stores them. An older income the WH-08 backfill has not derived yet is still served: its facts are read from its stored counterparty and the regime default (MODULE-withholdings §5.2, the backfill's own mapping) and its `withholding` is `null`, as is the `withholding` of one the rules cannot derive (backfill "need user input"); editing the record derives it. No deploy order is assumed. (A `$ref` keeps no sibling description: the strict response validator would drop the referenced properties.)
